# Wave W17-Y (Route 213): salt pine — a shore pine in deep salt-tolerant greens, tiered and wind-combed, its highlight lifted clear of the turf, on salt turf (ground baked in). Route 213’s own tree — split from Lake Gallant’s broad elm beside it by form entire (conifer shore vs broadleaf lakefront) and from Route 203’s dusted coal pine by air: salt wind here, mine smoke there.
